<title>THAILAND: Thai expressway firm in 8.5 bln baht loan deal.</title>
<headline>Thai expressway firm in 8.5 bln baht loan deal.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Industrial Finance Corp of Thailand said on Monday it and 10 financial institutions last week signed an 8.5 billion baht ($351.2 million) loan agreement with debt-ridden expressway operator Don Muang Tollway Co Ltd.</p>
<p>The loan requested by the finance ministry and signed on June 19 will be used to help overcome Don Muang's liquidity problems and repay existing debts, IFCT said in a statement.</p>
<p>It gave no further details.</p>
<p>IFCT is a development financial institution, majority owned by the finance ministry.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642 ($ = 24.2 Thai Baht)</p>
